## 4. Human Override System (HCAI)

The system supports three levels of human intervention:

### Level 1 — Direct Profile Editing
The user manually sets genre affinity values (e.g., Sci-Fi = 95%, Comedy = 5%).
The decoder translates this directly into movie scores without any AI correction.
The model acts purely as a genre-to-film translator.

```python
edited_profile[0, GENRES.index("Sci-Fi")] = 0.95
scores = model.recommend_from_edited_profile(edited_profile)
```

### Level 2 — Override Impact Transparency
After a user applies an override, the system shows which movies were most
boosted or suppressed, making the override's effect fully visible:

```python
impact = model.explain_override_impact(ann_output, final_output, idx_to_title)
# Returns: {"boosted": [...], "suppressed": [...]}
```

### Level 3 — Hybrid Override Path
The user expresses preferences in natural language categories
(`strongly_increase`, `slightly_reduce`, etc.), which are mapped to float
values and added as a genre-weighted bias on top of the AI output:

```python
override_tensor = build_override_tensor({"Sci-Fi": "strongly_increase"}, num_genres)
scores, profile = model(user_vector, user_overrides=override_tensor, alpha=3.0)
```

The override tensor is computed as:

```
explicit_bias = override_tensor @ M_genre     (1×18) @ (18×9742) → (1×9742)
final_output  = ann_output + α × explicit_bias
```

